+````markdown name=docs/runbooks/production_hardening_playbook.md
+```text
+Aegis Production Hardening Playbook — promote staging → production
+
+Scope
+- Harden Federated Learning control plane (Flower), Admission/Policy webhook, HSM/KMS rotation & signing, secure aggregation evaluation and DF (differential privacy) tuning.
+
+Assumptions
+- Kubernetes (staging) available and operator has cluster-admin for staging. For prod use limited admin and automation accounts.
+- cert-manager installed (or ability to create CA/TLS secrets).
+- Vault available and accessible from CI/operators.
+- MLflow server reachable and COSIGN key configured (KMS or Vault).
+- OAuth/OIDC provider available for oauth2-proxy or alternative auth.
+
+High Level Run Order (apply in staging first)
+1) Prep & inventory
+   - Ensure all secrets (COSIGN_KEY_REF, MLFLOW_DB_URL, EVIDENCE_BUCKET, OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET, VAULT token) are stored in Vault or k8s secrets referenced by Vault.
+   - Run tools/inventory_automation.py to capture current repo automation surface.
+
+2) RBAC, NetworkPolicy, PodSecurity
+   - Apply least-privilege RBAC for Flower and webhook services.
+     kubectl apply -f services/fl/secure/rbac-restricted.yaml -n aegis
+   - Apply NetworkPolicy to restrict inbound traffic to oauth2-proxy and webhook:
+     kubectl apply -f services/fl/secure/networkpolicy.yaml -n aegis
+   - Enforce PodSecurity Admission (restricted) on aegis namespace (cluster operator).
+
+3) TLS & Ingress
+   - Install cert-manager (if not present).
+   - Provision CA or use cert-manager ClusterIssuer (ACME/internal PKI).
+   - Apply flower certificate & ingress:
+     kubectl apply -f services/fl/secure/clusterissuer-selfsigned.yaml
+     kubectl apply -f services/fl/secure/flower-certificate.yaml
+     kubectl apply -f services/fl/secure/flower-ingress.yaml
+   - Verify TLS served:
+     curl -v https://flower.aegis.local/health --cacert <ca.pem>
+
+4) Auth (OIDC / oauth2-proxy)
+   - Deploy oauth2-proxy configured with your IdP.
+     kubectl apply -f services/fl/secure/oauth2-proxy-deployment.yaml -n aegis
+   - Validate login flow and that Flower endpoints require auth.
+
+5) Admission webhook (policy enforcement)
+   - Create CA, sign server cert, create k8s secret (see ops/webhook/generate_ca.sh).
+   - Deploy webhook server (ops/webhook/deploy_webhook.yaml).
+   - Generate ValidatingWebhookConfiguration with CA bundle (ops/webhook/generate_vwc.sh).
+   - Test webhook behavior by submitting Job manifests annotated carbon/sensitivity=high; expect rejection unless nodeSelector present.
+
+6) HSM/KMS & cosign
+   - Run HSM activation dry-run (ops/hsm/aws_hsm_activation_and_rotation_drill.sh).
+   - Verify cosign can sign with configured KMS/COSIGN_KEY_REF.
+   - Run a rotation drill in staging with audit officer present and record manifests to evidence bucket.
+
+7) FL Hardening
+   - Deploy Flower with serviceaccount aegis-flower-sa.
+   - Enforce ingress + oauth2-proxy + networkpolicy.
+   - Configure client enrollment workflow (ops/fl/register_client.py) so only registered/attested clients participate.
+   - Decide DP policy (epsilon target), run privacy tuning study (services/fl/privacy_tune/) and set DP defaults in FL client images.
+   - Decide secure aggregation plan and if cryptographic aggregator is required, schedule integration.
+
+8) Causal & Policy gating
+   - Ensure experiments must be approved and contain a preanalysis plan before deployment changes:
+     - Use ops/experiments/check_approval.py in CI.
+   - Policy CI gate: .github/workflows/policy_ci.yml will run tools/policy_ci_gate.py on PRs that enable agentic flows.
+
+9) Carbon control & measurement
+   - Start CodeCarbon instrumentation in training jobs; expose exporter (services/observability/carbon_exporter.py) to Prometheus.
+   - Label low-carbon nodepools using ops/k8s/label_nodepool.sh and enforce via admission webhook for heavy jobs.
+
+Verification & Smoke Tests
+- Run FL demo locally and in staging (demo/run_fl_demo_local.sh).
+- Run causal full pipeline CI to ensure registry & DoWhy flows (.github/workflows/causal_full_pipeline.yml).
+- Run CodeCarbon CI to capture carbon records (.github/workflows/codecarbon_ci.yml).
+- Run webhook validation: submit a Job annotated carbon/sensitivity=high and assert rejection if no nodeSelector carbon=green.
+
+Promote to production (gated)
+- Obtain signoff:
+  - Security signoff on TLS + RBAC + network policies
+  - Crypto/Auditor signoff on HSM/KMS processes
+  - ML privacy signoff (epsilon target approved)
+  - Sustainability signoff (carbon budgets)
+- Copy manifests to production-specific kustomize overlay, rotate secrets from staging to prod secrets, and run production rollout window.
+
+Rollback plan
+- If webhook blocks legitimate workloads, patch ValidatingWebhookConfiguration to set failurePolicy: Fail -> Ignore, then fix and re-enable Fail.
+- If Flower is unavailable, scale to 0 and re-route traffic to secondary control plane (if configured).
+
+Contacts & Escalation
+- Platform lead (pager), Crypto lead (HSM), Privacy lead (Opacus), Legal/Auditor (signoffs).
